{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "8171c2f5-96df-41f6-884c-dbd004ae8a17"/*ValueToRate*/,
  "Description": "Maps a value between 0 and 1 to one of the numbers in a list of rates.\n\nThe Rates string holds one number per line. Value 0 picks the first entry and values towards 1 pick the last; Value is clamped to that range. If the list is empty the result is 1.\n\nCan also be used with [MockStrings] to select between other groups of numbers such as primes.",
